# ontology-tutor

Deterministic ontology engineering for databases and folder systems. The skill teaches and applies TypeDB-grounded modeling primitives: entities, relations, attributes, roles, type hierarchies, ownership, inference, closed-world classification, and traceable design decisions. In mode 2, the skill additionally produces SQL Server-compatible embodiment of TypeDB design decisions with governed field-value review and operator-approved removal workflow.

## Contract Metadata

**`contract_version`:** `1.3.7`
**`supported_router_version`:** `1.2.1`

## Mode Selector

The operator declares the active mode at session start. Every validator invoked during the session must receive and honor the selected mode. If a validator cannot accept the selected mode, the agent must halt and report validator incompatibility — never silently use the wrong contract.

- **`mode = 1` — Pure TypeDB.** Validators apply Pure TypeDB expectations only. All existing commands operate in this mode by default.
- **`mode = 2` — TypeDB Embodiment using SQL.** Validators apply TypeDB intent plus SQL Server embodiment constraints. Adds SQL Embodiment commands, `field_value_test`, `field_review_matrix`, `proposed_removals`, `disagreements`, and `operator_decision` workflow to the session contract.

When no mode is declared by the operator, default to mode 1.

